[Music]  container registry is a private  container image registry that runs on  google cloud  this quick start shows you how to build  a docker image and how to push and pull  the image from your project's container  registry all from the command line  before you begin make sure that one you  have a google cloud project selected  two billing and the container registry  api are enabled and three you have the  cloud sdk and docker installed on your  docker file  which provides information on how to  package application two  requirements.txt  is used to list your application and  dependencies  three  app.pi is the actual python code of your  application  run the docker build command to create a  docker image on your local machine  next we'll configure docker to use the  gcloud command line tool to authenticate  requests to container registry using the  gcloud auth command now we use the  docker tag command to associate the  docker image with a registry name so  that we can push the image to a specific  location  we can now upload the docker image to  container registry with the docker push  command  you can view images hosted by container  registry via the google cloud console or  by visiting the images registry name in  your web browser  to pull the image from container  registry on your local machine run the  docker pool command  finally you can delete the docker image  from container registry using the gcloud  container images delete command  you

